  "live_records": {
    "q-81915": {
      "dom_id": "step-q81915",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14247468/assets/8f4a991a9da8b339bf2af1085787ba18227ee0926b1c280d8f3173f86c0713c8.png)\n\nCalculate the height $h$ of the cylinder above given that its volume is $32\\pi \\,{\\text{m}}^{3}$ and its radius is $2\\,\\text{m}.$",
      "worked_solution": "The volume of a cylinder with radius $r$ and height $h$ is given by\n\n$$\nV=\\pi {r}^{2}h.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $V=32\\pi \\,{\\text{m}}^{3}$ and $r=2\\,\\text{m}$ into the formula and solving for $r,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & =\\pi {r}^{2}h \\\\ 32\\pi  & =\\pi (2)^{2}h \\\\ 4\\pi h & =32\\pi  \\\\ h & =8\\,\\text{m}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
